    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis is about the beautiful youth of San Francisco, specifically the youth of Sunnydale and Bayview-Hunters Point. It amplifies their voices, brilliance, and experiences taking public transportation to and from school.\r\n\r\nPlease copy and paste this URL into your browser to watch the full abstract on YouTube:\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/Ma6Xcxb1DiU \r\n\r\nThis thesis was finished during the 2020 Pandemic COVID 19. The author finished it under great duress and personal struggle. The author finished it while watching the world finally acknowledge the cries of Black and Brown folks around the world.\r\n\r\nBlack Lives Matter. Love Heals All. Change Must Come. Listen. Empower. Envision. Dream. Share. Speak. Stand. Sing. Be You. Love Difference. See HUMANITY.\r\n\r\nThank you for your time <3",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Marquez, Lauren Elizabeth (2020). Building the Mothership: “School Bussing” on Public Transportation. Unpublished Honors Thesis. Stanford University, Stanford CA. https://purl.stanford.edu/mb673rs7926",
            "type": "preferred citation",
